{"reference":"Psalms 118","book":"Psalms","chapter":118,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Surrounding Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The psalms immediately preceding this one belong to a broader collection that holds together memories of sanctuary destruction and exile with thanksgiving after return, festival praise, meditation on Torah, and worship-oriented Songs of Ascents. This proposed setting is disputed, but it can help readers hear Psalm 118’s repeated thanksgiving and worship language within a larger pattern of communal praise.","verse_refs":["Psalms 113:1-9","Psalms 114:1-8","Psalms 115:1-18","Psalms 116:1-19","Psalms 117:1-2"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_118_7fc4eb349a71947b5728395c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}